# Legibility Office Research

## Purpose

This directory contains the research foundation of the Legibility Office Institutional Operating System (IOS).

The objective is to build an open institutional science that explains how governments develop long-term capability.

Research focuses on governance, procurement, Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI), AI governance, institutional memory, coordination, and national competitiveness.

---

# Research Themes

## Governance

Understanding how institutions coordinate authority, accountability, and public decision-making.

---

## Procurement

Exploring procurement as a strategic capability rather than an administrative process.

---

## Digital Public Infrastructure

Studying how identity, payments, interoperability, and digital public services strengthen institutional capability.

---

## Institutional Memory

Understanding how governments preserve knowledge, learn, and improve over time.

---

## AI Governance

Developing governance architectures that ensure AI strengthens institutional resilience.

---

## Institutional Capability

Measuring how institutions transform public investment into sustained productivity.

---

## Institutional Physics

Developing theoretical models explaining institutional behaviour, path dependence, governance inheritance, and capability formation.

---

# Research Outputs

The repository supports

